<LockabularyPage title="Lockabulary support" description="Help and contact for Lockabulary, the vocabulary trainer for iPhone and Mac." path="lockabulary">
  <h1>Learn a language, scroll less</h1>
  <p class="soft">Lockabulary is a vocabulary trainer for European Portuguese, Spanish and French. On iPhone it locks the apps you lose time in until you answer a few words. On Mac it lives in the menu bar and asks a few words every so often.</p>

  <div class="card">
    <p><strong>Something broke, or you have an idea?</strong></p>
    <p>Write to <a href="mailto:contact@arturwitkowski.com">contact@arturwitkowski.com</a>. The quickest way is Settings › Feedback in the app: a bug report brings the app's log along, which helps a lot.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>The lock on my iPhone doesn't start</h2>
  <p>Open Settings in Lockabulary and check three things: Screen Time access is allowed, at least one app is chosen under "Apps to lock", and the current time is inside your hours. "Test the lock" locks the chosen apps after 2 minutes of use, at any hour.</p>

  <h2>My progress isn't on my other device</h2>
  <p>Both devices need to be signed in to the same Apple Account with iCloud turned on. Progress syncs through your private iCloud database. "Sync now" in Settings asks for the latest right away.</p>

  <h2>One purchase, both devices</h2>
  <p>Lockabulary is a single purchase for iPhone and Mac. On the second device, download it from the App Store with the same Apple Account.</p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>No account, no ads, no analytics. Read the <a href="/lockabulary/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>
</LockabularyPage>
